{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"df4d5e3a-bfe0-4c83-a66f-c7706ab606a0","step":{"id":"s1","script":"A converging lens brings parallel rays toward the far focal point. Place an upright object twice the focal distance from the lens.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"title","region":"A1","content":"Converging lens: object at 2F"},{"op":"diagram","id":"lensdiagram","region":"right","primitives":[{"kind":"line","points":[[0.06,0.55],[0.94,0.55]],"stroke":"dashed","label":"principal axis"},{"kind":"ellipse","center":[0.5,0.55],"radius":[0.035,0.36],"stroke":"solid","label":"lens"},{"kind":"point","at":[0.35,0.55],"label":"F"},{"kind":"point","at":[0.65,0.55],"label":"F′"},{"kind":"line","points":[[0.2,0.55],[0.2,0.3]],"stroke":"solid","arrow":true,"label":"object"}]}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"df4d5e3a-bfe0-4c83-a66f-c7706ab606a0","step":{"id":"s2","script":"From the object tip, draw a ray parallel to the axis. After the lens, it passes through the far focal point.","ops":[{"op":"arrow","id":"parallelray","canvas_id":"lensdiagram","from":[0.2,0.3],"to":[0.5,0.3],"stroke":"solid"},{"op":"arrow","id":"focusedray","canvas_id":"lensdiagram","from":[0.5,0.3],"to":[0.8,0.8],"stroke":"solid"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"df4d5e3a-bfe0-4c83-a66f-c7706ab606a0","step":{"id":"s3","script":"A second ray passes straight through the thin lens center. Where the rays meet locates the inverted image tip.","ops":[{"op":"arrow","id":"centralray","canvas_id":"lensdiagram","from":[0.2,0.3],"to":[0.8,0.8],"stroke":"solid"},{"op":"arrow","id":"image","canvas_id":"lensdiagram","from":[0.8,0.55],"to":[0.8,0.8],"stroke":"solid","label":"image"}],"checkpoint":{"question":"Why is this image real rather than virtual?","expected_gist":"The actual outgoing rays meet, rather than only their backward extensions."}}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"df4d5e3a-bfe0-4c83-a66f-c7706ab606a0","step":{"id":"s4","script":"At twice the focal distance, the image forms twice the focal distance beyond the lens: real, inverted, and the same size.","ops":[{"op":"point","id":"objectdistance","canvas_id":"lensdiagram","at":[0.2,0.55],"label":"2F"},{"op":"point","id":"imagedistance","canvas_id":"lensdiagram","at":[0.8,0.55],"label":"2F′"},{"op":"equation","id":"distances","anchor":{"el":"title","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"d_o=2f\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad d_i=2f"},{"op":"equation","id":"magnification","anchor":{"el":"distances","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"m=-\\frac{d_i}{d_o}=-1"}],"checkpoint":null}}
